 received unattached to the specimen  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior black  posterior blue  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a well circumscribed partially gelatinous  partially necrotic cut surface  A 0 15cm rim of fibrous tissue encapsulates the mass  The mass is located 0 3cm from the blue inked margin   0 1cm from the green inked margin  0 1cm from the black inked margin  and 0 5cm from the yellow inked margin  An expansion of the fibrotic capsule surrounding the tumor brings this structure in direct opposition to the yellow inked surgical margin  Representative sections of two separate areas of the mass are frozen as FX 1 and FX 1A  FX 1 is resubmitted cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   FX 1A is kept frozen  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   FX 1 Representative section of tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections through tumor demonstrating proximity to black inked surgical margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections through the tumor demonstrates proximity to blue inked surgical margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections through tumor demonstrating proximity to yellow inked surgical margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections through tumor demonstrating proximity to green inked surgical margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of the tumor Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass final shaved margins   is a hollow shell of fibrofatty tissue which measures 12 x 9 x 8cm in overall dimension which has numerous sutures placed to designate the outer aspect of the specimen which represents the true surgical margin of the resection bed  The new true surgical margin is inked black and the specimen is serial sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  Representative sections of the tissue involving the black inked surgical margin are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATI