Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Breast CTR Surg WAC 240 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  JENNIFER BELMONTE  PA HELENANNE D ALESSANDRO  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is 51 year old woman with two areas of calcifications in the right breast  The first is at 12 00 o clock  The second area is inferior to the 12 00 o clock area  The 12 00 o clock calcifications are adjacent to an area of architectural distortion which has remained stable  The differential diagnosis includes ductal carcinoma in situ and fibrocystic changes  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  RIGHT  12 00   CORE BIOPSY 1  ATYPICAL PAPILLARY DUCT LESION WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SEE NOTE  B  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR   CORE BIOPSY 1  RADIAL SCAR WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  2  MODERATE USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SEE NOTE  Note  Sections of the core biopsy of the right breast at 12 0 o clock  part A  reveal a complex sclerosing papillary duct lesion composed of fibrovascular cores lined by monomorphic ductal cells with low grade cytologic atypia  Although a diagnosis of intraductal papilloma is favored  excision of the lesion to fully characterize the process is recommended as clinically indicated  Sections of the core biopsy of the right breast  inferior to 12 00 o clock  part B  reveal a focal radial scar with areas of usual ductal hyperplasia and associated calcifications  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the myoepithelial layer and supports the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  both of which are labeled Lana Schofield   333 39 83  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast spec 12 o clock     removed from a blue cassette  are 4 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right breast inferior spec B     removed from a blue cassette  is an aggregate of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received in the same container is an aggregate of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 02   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09 00 27PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right 12 00   Core biopsy PART B  Breast  Right  Inferior   Core biopsy  report_end  , no_InvasiveSuspicious.
